            <div xml:id="d438">

                <pb facs="0380" n="368" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg368"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.7962/112a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wharton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-13T21:00:00-04:00">March 13, 1942—9
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>54. For McBride. Please telegraph what measures can in your opinion be taken to
                    exercise censorship in Liberia regarding present <pb facs="0381" n="369"
                        xml:id="pg369"/> and future plans and operations of American forces,
                    including particularly activities at the airport. War Department understands
                    that Associated Press maintains a correspondent in Monrovia, believed to be the
                    wife of a Firestone employee.</p>
                <p>You may in your discretion discuss this subject with President Barclay.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
